# SmartKontrakt / Kiln — environment variables.
#
# Copy to `.env` for local use. `.env*` is gitignored (this example is not).
# Nothing here is required to run locally: with no DATABASE_URL the app uses an
# embedded PGLite database, and with no OPENROUTER_API_KEY the audit still
# completes using the deterministic template review.

# ── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Server-only. Prefer the Vercel Supabase integration, which sets these for you:
#   POSTGRES_PRISMA_URL, POSTGRES_URL, POSTGRES_URL_NON_POOLING
# src/lib/db.ts reads DATABASE_URL first, then the integration vars (pooler
# order). Leave unset for the local embedded PGLite database.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:<password>@<host>:5432/postgres

# ── AI review (OpenRouter) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Server-only, never a browser variable. Without a key, reviews fall back to the
# template review (report.aiStatus = "unavailable").
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...
# Any OpenRouter model id. Default: nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=

# ── Public app URL ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used as the HTTP-Referer on OpenRouter calls. On Vercel, VERCEL_URL is picked
# up automatically; set this only for a custom domain.
# APP_URL=https://your-app.example.com

# ── Optional access control ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The app has no sign-in. Set this to require the shared secret in the
# `x-kiln-admin-token` header on every mutating server function (save, delete,
# AI calls, database-config changes). Unset => the app is open, as before.
# The browser attaches the header automatically once the same value is stored:
#   localStorage.setItem("kiln_admin_token", "<the token>")
# KILN_ADMIN_TOKEN=

# The pipeline worker (pipeline-worker/) reads its OWN .env — see
# pipeline-worker/.env.example — and talks to the database directly.
